cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ZDepth, please cite it as below. It was co-created with generative AI; see the README's 'Credits and AI disclosure'."
type: software
title: "ZDepth: a depth (z-buffer) pass for Rhino 8"
version: 0.9.1-beta
date-released: 2026-10-22
authors:
  - alias: adpchrgruber
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/adpchrgruber/ZDepth_Rh8_Mac"
abstract: >-
  Rhino 8 plug-in that shows the depth pass (z-buffer) live in the viewport and saves
  exact depth maps as 8-bit PNG, 16-bit PNG or float EXR at any size, rendered on the CPU
  from the objects the view shows. Works on the Mac, where Rhino's ShowZBuffer does not.
  Developed with generative AI assistance (Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code, Anthropic),
  directed, reviewed and tested by the author.
keywords:
  - Rhino
  - RhinoCommon
  - depth map
  - z-buffer
  - compositing
  - ControlNet
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Claude (Opus 5.5 version)"
    authors:
      - name: Anthropic
    year: 2026
    url: "https://www.anthropic.com/claude"
    notes: "Large language model; wrote code and documentation for ZDepth."
  - type: software
    title: "Claude Code"
    authors:
      - name: Anthropic
    year: 2026
    url: "https://claude.com/claude-code"
    notes: "Coding agent used to develop ZDepth."
